      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "I favor \"undefined\" for consistency with the aggregate rules in the standard calling convention.\r\n\r\nConsistency with the treatment of other integer types, and following the _logic_ used in aapcs, suggests type-sign extension up to 32 bits and sign extension to XLEN.  Ideally, we would have empirical data from at least one real-world application before committing to this decision.\r\n\r\nThe sizes and alignments look reasonable to me.",
