    "body": "It looks a bit unnatural to store the limbs/chunks on big-endian systems in low-endian order.\r\n@kito-cheng Please, check what is done on other big-endian architectures like s390x, powerpc, arm.\r\n\r\nGemini gave me this response but , please, check in code.\r\n\r\n**mp_limb_t and Endianness**\r\nOn a big-endian system (like s390x or PowerPC), the mp_limb_t array is stored from most significant limb to least significant limb. For example, for a 1024-bit number, the most significant 64-bit word would be at the lowest address of the array, and the least significant word would be at the highest address.",
